; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1978  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1979  ** Parameters(in)   : ErrorType                                               **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1980  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1981  ** Parameters (out) : None                                                    **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1982  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1983  ** Return value     : None                                                    **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1984  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1985  ** Description      : This is an Error handler function which can be called   **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1986                        in two conditions                                       **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1987  ** 1. Any detection of inconsistency in copies of relevant global variables   **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1988  **    is reported to the user via the function Mcal_SafeErrorHandler.         **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1989  **    Mcal_SafeErrorHandler shall never return, else it may lead to           **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1990  **    unpredictable behavior.The user is expected to perform the error        **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1991  **    handling in this function.                                              **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1992  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1993  **    The error reported is MCAL_DIV_INCONSISTENCY:Typical error reactions    **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1994  **    could be to reset the microcontroller (software reset)                  **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1995  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1996  ** 2. Support functions are called to access the protected registers,         **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1997  **    these functions can be called from multiple cores concurrently, a       **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1998  **    spinlock mechanism with timeout is provided. In case, the timeout       **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  1999  **    expires, it is reported to the user via Mcal_SafeErrorHandler.          **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2000  **    The user is expected to perform the error handling in this function.    **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2001  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2002  **    The error reported is MCAL_SPINLOCK_TIMEOUT:Typical error reactions     **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2003  **    could be to the terminate the operating system task or restart the      **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2004  **    partition or reset the microcontroller.                                 **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2005  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2006  **    This funtion is written here only to avoid build error.                 **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2007  **    The user needs to implement this functionality (Mcal_SafeErrorHandler)  **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2008  **    in a separate file and needs to add this file as part of the build.     **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2009  **                                                                            **
; ..\_03_MCAL\Src\Mcal\src\Mcal.c	  2010  *******************************************************************************/
